ice frame the contest, and every major race rater calls it Solid or Safe Democratic. Prediction markets price a Becerra win near 96 percent, and a New York Times report describes him holding wide polling leads.\n\nHilton, a British-born former adviser turned commentator, has slightly outraised Becerra, $7.3 million to $6.1 million, and the two clashed in their only scheduled debate on October 1, with much of the exchange centered on Trump. Coverage of the debate generally favored Becerra, and Hilton calls himself the underdog. Nothing in the recent record suggests the state's structural Democratic advantage has eroded enough to put the outcome in doubt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 17.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9982, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9936, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9916, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9808, "margin": 14.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9828, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9795, "margin": 14.0}]}